  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, tells of Lewis Branscomb, then head of the National Bureau of Standards, a US government science agency. Michels says Branscomb allegedly offered Edward Condon, a physicist who chaired a 1960s committee studying UFOs, a deal: help bury the UFO question and get back his security clearance, meaning his permission to see secret information. If true, it would mean the government's official UFO study was steered toward a set answer."
